     "execution_count": 39,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Was the price below $3.00 in each week?\n",
    "gas_prices < 3.00"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "83505d60",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The real power comes from the fact that Python treats `True` as 1 and `False` as 0. That means we can *count* how many weeks met our condition by summing the boolean array, and find the *proportion* of weeks by taking its mean:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 40,
   "id": "f5673d66",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "np.int64(5)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 40,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# How many weeks was gas below $3.00?\n",
    "np.sum(gas_prices < 3.00)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "e95a42bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "np.float64(0.09615384615384616)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 41,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# What fraction of weeks was gas below $3.00?\n",
    "np.mean(gas_prices < 3.00)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b64d311",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Gas dipped below \\$3.00 in only 5 of the 52 weeks, or about 10% of the year. We can build more specific conditions by combining comparisons with `&` (\"and\") and `|` (\"or\"). Each comparison must be wrapped in parentheses:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "id": "df6edbc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "np.int64(45)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 42,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# How many weeks was the price between $3.00 and $3.20?\n",
    "np.sum((gas_prices > 3.00) & (gas_prices < 3.20))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35cee90e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Boolean indexing\n",
    "\n",
    "Beyond counting, we can use a boolean array to *pull out* the values that meet a condition. This is called **boolean indexing** or **masking**:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "6c0ea6b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "array([2.985, 2.94 , 2.895, 2.841, 2.811])"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 43,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The actual prices for the weeks when gas was below $3.00\n",
    "gas_prices[gas_prices < 3.00]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4295e1d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The full value of masking appears when you then summarize the selected values. For example, *among the weeks when gas was below \\$3.00*, what was the average price?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "id": "5d168271",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "np.float64(2.8944)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 44,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "np.mean(gas_prices[gas_prices < 3.00])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5c1a1d02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
