   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The shape `(512, 512)` tells us the photo is 512 pixels tall and 512 pixels wide, with a single brightness value at each position, just like the small example above. The data type `uint8` is an unsigned 8-bit integer: `u` means no negative values, and 8 bits gives exactly 256 possible values, from 0 to 255. Here 0 is black and 255 is white.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Color images are 3D arrays\n",
    "\n",
    "Color photographs add a third dimension. Here we load a photo of bell peppers:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 61,
   "id": "78418b6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 672x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
